# Agent tooling. Not part of the product, and not published with it.
#
# It was tracked for a while, on the argument that a hook deciding what leaves
# this machine is a security control and belongs under review. The owner's call
# is that development tooling stays on the machine it runs on. Nothing is
# deleted locally — this only stops it being uploaded.
#
# `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/` are listed for a second reason as well. Instructions
# written for an assistant are not documentation of this project, and if they
# ever contradict what the repository can demonstrate — the accounts, the
# checks, what the merge bar accepts and refuses — the repository is the record
# and they are not. Keeping them unversioned means `git add -A` cannot make one
# look like the other.
.claude/
apps/web/AGENTS.md
apps/web/CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.agents/

# Backups are evidence of a drill, not artefacts of the repository.
.backups/
